WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.421
My name is William Crabtree. I was a young boy in England in the year 1800.

2
00:00:06.422 --> 00:00:11.891
In those days some people became very rich by putting machines into factories.

3
00:00:11.892 --> 00:00:15.202
This change was called the Industrial Revolution.

4
00:00:15.203 --> 00:00:20.005
Before machines were invented, all the work had to be done by hand.

5
00:00:20.006 --> 00:00:25.058
But with machines, things could be done much more quickly.

6
00:00:25.059 --> 00:00:29.989
This was wonderful for the factory owners, but it was awful for the workers.

7
00:00:29.990 --> 00:00:33.792
The machines were dangerous and created a lot of dirt.

8
00:00:33.793 --> 00:00:38.310
Even worse, the factory owners treated the workers very badly.

9
00:00:38.311 --> 00:00:43.140
The owners only cared about their money and their machines.

10
00:00:43.141 --> 00:00:48.857
In those days a man was paid about ten shillings a day, which is less than one dollar.

11
00:00:48.858 --> 00:00:56.576
However, children were paid only two shillings a day, so the owners liked to hire poor children to work in their factories.

12
00:00:56.577 --> 00:00:58.558
It was terrible work.

13
00:00:58.559 --> 00:01:04.989
I began working in a textile factory when I was eight years old.

14
00:01:04.990 --> 00:01:08.804
A textile factory is a factory that makes cloth.

15
00:01:08.805 --> 00:01:12.796
My family was so poor that I could not go to school.

16
00:01:12.797 --> 00:01:15.980
I had to earn money so that we could live.

17
00:01:15.981 --> 00:01:19.791
I worked every day from six in the morning to ten at night.

18
00:01:19.792 --> 00:01:24.438
Even on Sundays I had to go to the factory to clean all the machines.

19
00:01:24.439 --> 00:01:27.948
It was very hard labor.

20
00:01:27.949 --> 00:01:32.607
I was so tired at night that I sometimes slept as I walked home.

21
00:01:32.608 --> 00:01:37.278
When people saw me walking home, they would tell me to quit my job.

22
00:01:37.279 --> 00:01:42.198
But I couldn't because my father's wages were not enough to feed our family.

23
00:01:42.199 --> 00:01:48.677
When I got home at night, I was always hungry, but usually I was too tired to eat my dinner.

24
00:01:48.678 --> 00:01:53.676
I would just fall down and sleep.

25
00:01:53.677 --> 00:01:56.864
Sometimes in the morning, I could not wake up.

26
00:01:56.865 --> 00:02:01.162
So my father would carry me to the factory while I was still sleeping.

27
00:02:01.163 --> 00:02:06.600
But I couldn't be late. If I were late for work, I would be in big trouble.

28
00:02:06.601 --> 00:02:15.187
My friend David was often late for work, so the owner often beat him with a strap.

29
00:02:15.188 --> 00:02:22.699
I was a piecer. All day I had to lean over the spinning machine, which was the machine that made the cloth.

30
00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:26.769
Piecers had to tie pieces of thread together when they broke.

31
00:02:26.770 --> 00:02:30.882
If the thread was broken, the machine could not make the cloth.

32
00:02:30.883 --> 00:02:36.213
So it was very important for us to do our job correctly.

33
00:02:36.214 --> 00:02:39.961
We were always running, and we could never sit down.

34
00:02:39.962 --> 00:02:43.358
It was very difficult to keep up with the work.

35
00:02:43.359 --> 00:02:48.426
We also had to work quickly. The owner also beat slow children.

36
00:02:48.427 --> 00:02:55.389
We were all very afraid of him. He was a bad man.

37
00:02:55.390 --> 00:03:00.401
A piecer's work was dangerous. We had to put our hands into the machine.

38
00:03:00.402 --> 00:03:05.130
If a piecer fell or was too slow, very bad things could happen.

39
00:03:05.131 --> 00:03:09.224
Many of my friends got badly hurt, and some even died.

40
00:03:09.225 --> 00:03:12.958
We had to be very careful.

41
00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:16.317
The worst part of working at the factory was the food.

42
00:03:16.318 --> 00:03:22.797
We were given only a little bit of soup and some bad-tasting bread for breakfast, lunch, and dinner.

43
00:03:22.798 --> 00:03:25.366
And we were not allowed to stop working.

44
00:03:25.367 --> 00:03:30.724
We had to eat our meals standing at the machines.

45
00:03:30.725 --> 00:03:37.430
Since the machines were very dirty, my food was often covered in dirt, so I had to eat dirty food.

46
00:03:37.431 --> 00:03:42.419
This made me very sick. One time a boy complained about the food.

47
00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:49.671
The owner got very angry with him. After that, no one ever complained again.

48
00:03:49.672 --> 00:03:55.089
Around 1833 some good men in the government tried to help the children.

49
00:03:55.090 --> 00:04:01.018
A new law made it illegal in England for a child under ten to work in a textile factory,

50
00:04:01.019 --> 00:04:06.062
and children under twelve could work no more than eight or ten hours a day.

51
00:04:06.063 --> 00:04:13.560
Also, on Sundays, the factory owners had to teach the children to read and write.

52
00:04:13.561 --> 00:04:19.063
As time passed, new laws were passed to improve the lives of children even more.

53
00:04:19.064 --> 00:04:25.154
In 1867 the laws on child labor were extended to many more industries.

54
00:04:25.155 --> 00:04:29.255
It became illegal in England to hire children to work in mines,

55
00:04:29.256 --> 00:04:36.220
at shipyards, and many dangerous factories, such as match factories and nail factories.

56
00:04:36.221 --> 00:04:41.467
Today almost every country in the world has child labor laws to protect children.

57
00:04:41.468 --> 00:04:47.199
In 1990 the United Nations agreed on the Convention on the Rights of the Child,

58
00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:52.805
which protects children not just from unfair work, but from war and disease.

59
00:04:52.806 --> 00:04:58.107
It also protects the right of children to live with their parents and go to school.

60
00:04:58.108 --> 00:05:01.810
Attitudes have changed greatly since the 1880s.

61
00:05:01.811 --> 00:05:07.932
Today childhood is cherished as a time to grow and learn in health and safety.

